flex for OpenVMS
================

This is flex @VERSION@, the fast lexical analyser generator, built natively
for OpenVMS @ARCH@ from the unmodified release plus the patches in the
vms-flex project:

    https://github.com/issinoho/vms-flex

Kit version: @KITVERSION@.  flex is free software under a BSD-style
licence; see COPYING.  The manual is FLEX.TXT; FLEX.1 is the manual page;
WC.L is a small example scanner (a word counter).

flex needs GNU m4 at run time: the M4 kit (https://github.com/issinoho/vms-m4)
is a prerequisite.

What is installed
-----------------
    FLEX$ROOT:[BIN]FLEX.EXE             flex
    FLEX$ROOT:[LIB]LIBFL.OLB            yywrap() and main() for scanners
                                        compiled with the default
                                        /NAMES=(UPPERCASE,TRUNCATED)
    FLEX$ROOT:[LIB]LIBFL_AS_IS.OLB      the same, for /NAMES=(AS_IS,SHORTENED)
    FLEX$ROOT:[INCLUDE]FLEXLEXER.H      the header for C++ scanners
    FLEX$ROOT:[000000]FLEX$SETUP.COM    defines the flex command
    FLEX$ROOT:[DOC]                     this file, COPYING, NEWS, FLEX.TXT,
                                        FLEX.1, WC.L
    SYS$STARTUP:FLEX$STARTUP.COM        defines FLEX$ROOT

Setting up
----------
The kit installs FLEX$STARTUP.COM into SYS$STARTUP and runs it once.  To
define FLEX$ROOT at every boot, the system manager adds this line to
SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM, after the one for M4$STARTUP.COM:

    $ @SYS$STARTUP:FLEX$STARTUP.COM

Each user (or SYLOGIN.COM, for everyone) then defines the command:

    $ @FLEX$ROOT:[000000]FLEX$SETUP.COM

Using flex
----------
    $ flex --header-file=wc.h -o wc.c wc.l
    $ cc wc.c
    $ link wc, FLEX$ROOT:[LIB]LIBFL/LIBRARY

Link a scanner compiled with /NAMES=(AS_IS,SHORTENED) with LIBFL_AS_IS.OLB
instead; a scanner that defines its own yywrap() (or uses
%option noyywrap) and main() needs neither.  Name the output with -o: the
default name, lex.yy.c, needs an ODS-5 disk.  -t writes the scanner to
SYS$OUTPUT.

flex runs m4 as M4$ROOT:[BIN]M4.EXE; the logical name (or environment
variable) M4 overrides it.  m4 runs in a subprocess when flex has written
the scanner, with its input and output in temporary files in SYS$SCRATCH.

Upper-case options and batch jobs
---------------------------------
Under the TRADITIONAL DCL parse style DCL upper-cases the unquoted parts of
a command and the C run-time library passes them to flex in lower case, so
an unquoted -B (batch) arrives as -b (backing-up report), -I as -i, -L as
-l and -Cf as -cf.  Batch jobs use TRADITIONAL even when interactive logins
are set to EXTENDED.  Use the long options (--batch, --noline), quote the
short ones ("-B"), or start the procedure with

    $ SET PROCESS/PARSE_STYLE=EXTENDED

Exit status
-----------
Under DCL a failed run exits with an error-severity status, so ON ERROR and
IF .NOT. $STATUS work; flex's exit code N is ($STATUS .AND. %X7F8) / 8.
Under a GNV shell, $? is the exit code as on Unix.
